Yes.
Before testing full orchestration using Airflow DAG, first stop ALL manually running services.

Then DAG itself will:

* start Zookeeper
* start Kafka
* start Expansion Service
* start Event Generator
* start Event Enricher
* start Beam/Dataflow job
* validate BigQuery

Follow EXACTLY these steps.

---

# STEP 1 — Stop Beam Pipeline

```bash
pkill -f beam_pipeline1.py
```

Verify:

```bash
ps -ef | grep beam_pipeline
```

Should show only:

```text
grep beam_pipeline
```

---

# STEP 2 — Stop Event Generator

```bash
pkill -f event_generator1.py
```

Verify:

```bash
ps -ef | grep event_generator
```

---

# STEP 3 — Stop Event Enricher

```bash
pkill -f event_enricher1.py
```

Verify:

```bash
ps -ef | grep event_enricher
```

---

# STEP 4 — Stop Expansion Service

```bash
pkill -f expansion-service
```

OR:

```bash
pkill java
```

Verify:

```bash
jps
```

Expansion service should disappear.

---

# STEP 5 — Stop Kafka

```bash
pkill -f kafka.Kafka
```

Verify:

```bash
jps
```

Kafka should disappear.

---

# STEP 6 — Stop Zookeeper

```bash
pkill -f QuorumPeerMain
```

Verify:

```bash
jps
```

Now ideally only:

```text
Jps
```

should appear.

---

# STEP 7 — Verify Everything Stopped

Run:

```bash
jps
```

Expected:

```text
12345 Jps
```

ONLY.

---

# STEP 8 — Copy DAG To Airflow DAGs Folder

```bash
cp ~/realtime_pipeline_monitoring.py ~/airflow/dags/
```

Verify:

```bash
ls ~/airflow/dags
```

You should see:

```text
realtime_pipeline_monitoring.py
```

---

# STEP 9 — Start Airflow Scheduler

Open terminal:

```bash
source ~/airflow-env/bin/activate

airflow scheduler
```

Keep running.

---

# STEP 10 — Start Airflow Webserver

Open NEW terminal:

```bash
source ~/airflow-env/bin/activate

airflow webserver --port 8080
```

Keep running.

---

# STEP 11 — Open Airflow UI

Browser:

```text
http://YOUR_VM_IP:8080
```

OR local VM:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

---

# STEP 12 — Enable DAG

Find DAG:

```text
realtime_pipeline_monitoring
```

Turn ON toggle.

---

# STEP 13 — Trigger DAG

Click:

```text
▶ Trigger DAG
```

---

# STEP 14 — Monitor DAG Tasks

You should see tasks running in order:

```text
start_zookeeper
↓
start_kafka
↓
start_expansion_service
↓
start_generator
↓
start_enricher
↓
start_beam_pipeline
↓
monitor_dataflow
↓
validate_bigquery
```

---

# STEP 15 — Verify Dataflow

Open:

```text
GCP Console → Dataflow
```

You should see:

```text
advanced-kafka-analytics-vX
```

Running.

---

# STEP 16 — Verify BigQuery

Run:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM `project-6e64a1a1-8e69-4a88-93d.realtime_analytics.streaming_metrics`
ORDER BY processing_time DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

You should see fresh rows loading.

